const faqs = [
  ["What is alcohol addiction?", "Alcohol addiction, also called alcohol dependence or alcohol use disorder (AUD), is a chronic medical condition that affects how the brain regulates impulse control, reward pathways, and stress responses. Over time, alcohol use can become compulsive or difficult to control, even when it causes harm to health, relationships, or daily functioning. AUD can range from mild to severe and may include physical dependence, withdrawal symptoms, cravings, and increased tolerance. The condition is highly treatable with the right blend of medical, psychological, and behavioral support."],
  ["How do I know if my drinking is a problem?", "If you drink more than you mean to, can’t cut back, or drinking is causing problems at home, work or with your health, it may be time to get help."],
  ["Is it safe to stop drinking on my own?", "Not always. If you drink heavily or daily, stopping suddenly can cause serious withdrawal. Talk to a medical provider first; we can help you find medical detox."],
  ["Do I need detox before starting?", "It depends on how much and how often you drink. Our admissions team will help you decide and arrange it if needed."],
  ["Do you provide detox or residential treatment?", "Hopewell Health Solutions is an outpatient practice. If a higher level of care such as detox or residential treatment is needed, our team helps coordinate that referral, and supports you when you step back down to outpatient care."],
  ["Are there medications for alcohol addiction?", "Yes. Some medications reduce cravings or help prevent relapse, and our providers can review options with you through <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/treatment-methods/medication-assisted-treatment/\">medication-assisted treatment</a>. When appropriate, our psychiatric team may recommend FDA-approved medications to reduce cravings, support abstinence, or ease withdrawal, alongside therapy and other support."],
  ["Do you offer an addiction IOP or PHP for alcohol?", "Yes. Our <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/addiction-iop/\">Addiction and Substance Use IOP</a> (Glastonbury and Westbrook) and our addiction PHP (Glastonbury) both treat alcohol addiction. Many clients step down into them after inpatient rehab or detox."],
  ["Can I keep working during treatment?", "Yes. Our addiction IOP is designed to fit around work."],
  ["What if I drink because of anxiety or depression?", "Our <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/adult-mental-health-iop/\">Co-Occurring IOP</a> treats both together."],
  ["How can I help a family member who drinks too much?", "Call us with them or on their behalf. We’ll talk through options and how to start the conversation."],
  ["Is treatment in person or virtual?", "Both, in person at our Downtown Glastonbury and Westbrook offices or by secure telehealth, with evening and daytime scheduling options."],
  ["Does insurance cover alcohol treatment?", "Most commercial plans do, including most major PPO plans. We <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/rates-and-insurance-coverage/\">check your benefits for free</a>. We don’t accept Medicare or Medicaid / HUSKY."],
  ["Is treatment confidential?", "Yes. Federal law gives addiction treatment records extra privacy protection."],
];
